cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Git Commit Migrator — Ghost Commits & GitHub Contribution Graph Sync"
message: "If you use or reference this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Cesar
    family-names: Ovies
    alias: CesarOvies
repository-code: "https://github.com/CesarOvies/GitCommitMigrator"
url: "https://cesarovies.github.io/GitCommitMigrator/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Dual-platform utility (100% client-side Web SPA and Windows .NET 8 Portable Desktop application)
  that extracts Git commit metadata by author email from local or remote repositories (GitHub, GitLab,
  Bitbucket, Azure DevOps) and reconstructs the contribution history in a personal repository using
  empty Ghost Commits. Preserves GitHub contribution graphs (green squares), commit dates, and messages
  without exposing proprietary source code, files, or secrets.
keywords:
  - git
  - github
  - ghost-commits
  - empty-commits
  - github-contribution-graph
  - green-squares
  - commit-migrator
  - git-history-migration
  - work-to-personal-github
  - gitlab-to-github
  - bitbucket-to-github
  - libgit2sharp
  - isomorphic-git
  - privacy
  - developer-tools

